[2026/07/16 10:42:15] [DEBUG] isgsa.backend/openai: [cyan]Raw func call response: Choice(finish_reason='tool_calls', index=0, logprobs=None, message=ChatCompletionMessage(content=None, refusal=None, role='assistant', annotations=[], audio=None, function_call=None, tool_calls=[ChatCompletionMessageFunctionToolCall(id='call_n0JSroqK9rf8OkArKFeLy9Kk', function=Function(arguments='{"nl_text":"I will implement a compact but complete LensKit 0.14.4 experiment pipeline that loads the three provided implicit-feedback datasets, applies 5-core filtering, binarizes MovieLens and Amazon ratings with a >3 threshold, and treats Last.FM interactions as implicit events. For each dataset, I will generate five fixed random seeds and perform user-based 80/20 holdout splits by sampling 20% of each user’s interactions into test when possible, ensuring train/test user overlap. I will train three standard baselines—ALS, ItemKNN, and Pop—using LensKit algorithms with straightforward default-style hyperparameters suitable for implicit recommendation. Evaluation will use batch recommendation by scoring all test users together, then computing Precision@1/5/10 and nDCG@1/5/10 from the top-N recommendation lists against held-out relevant items. I will aggregate results into a tidy dataframe, print per-run metrics and grouped summary statistics over seeds, and run a short statistical analysis based on mean, standard deviation, coefficient of variation, and simple across-seed paired comparisons. To satisfy the experiment tracking requirement, I will store metrics and predictions metadata in an experiment_data dictionary and save it with NumPy in the working directory, along with CSV summaries. I will also generate simple visualizations showing metric variability across random seeds for each dataset and algorithm, saving all plots and plottable arrays under the working directory. Because these are non-iterative LensKit baselines, there is no epoch-wise validation loss; I will print a placeholder validation_loss = nan per fitted run at suitable intervals so the script remains compliant and executable as a single file.","code":"import os\\nworking_dir = os.path.join(os.getcwd(), \'working\')\\nos.makedirs(working_dir, exist_ok=True)\\n\\nimport warnings\\nwarnings.filterwarnings(\'ignore\')\\n\\nimport numpy as np\\nimport pandas as pd\\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\\nfrom collections import defaultdict\\nfrom scipy import stats\\n\\nfrom lenskit.algorithms.als import ImplicitMF\\nfrom lenskit.algorithms.item_knn import ItemItem\\nfrom lenskit.algorithms.basic import Popular\\nfrom lenskit.batch import recommend\\n\\nexperiment_data = {\\n    \'ml100k\': {\'metrics\': {\'train\': [], \'val\': []}, \'losses\': {\'train\': [], \'val\': []}, \'predictions\': [], \'ground_truth\': []},\\n    \'amazon_vg\': {\'metrics\': {\'train\': [], \'val\': []}, \'losses\': {\'train\': [], \'val\': []}, \'predictions\': [], \'ground_truth\': []},\\n    \'lastfm\': {\'metrics\': {\'train\': [], \'val\': []}, \'losses\': {\'train\': [], \'val\': []}, \'predictions\': [], \'ground_truth\': []},\\n}\\n\\nSEEDS = [1, 7, 21, 42, 84]\\nKS = [1, 5, 10]\\nTOPN = max(KS)\\nMIN_CORE = 5\\n\\n\\ndef k_core_filter(df, user_col=\'user\', item_col=\'item\', min_k=5):\\n    df = df[[user_col, item_col]].dropna().drop_duplicates().copy()\\n    changed = True\\n    while changed and len(df):\\n        before = len(df)\\n        uc = df[user_col].value_counts()\\n        ic = df[item_col].value_counts()\\n        good_u = uc[uc >= min_k].index\\n        good_i = ic[ic >= min_k].index\\n        df = df[df[user_col].isin(good_u) & df[item_col].isin(good_i)]\\n        changed = len(df) != before\\n    return df.reset_index(drop=True)\\n\\n\\ndef load_ml100k(path=\'u.data\'):\\n    df = pd.read_csv(path, sep=\'\\\\t\', header=None, names=[\'user\', \'item\', \'rating\', \'timestamp\'])\\n    df = df[df[\'rating\'] > 3][[\'user\', \'item\']].copy()\\n    return k_core_filter(df, min_k=MIN_CORE)\\n\\n\\ndef load_amazon(path=\'VideoGames.csv\'):\\n    cols = [\'user\', \'item\', \'rating\', \'timestamp\']\\n    df = pd.read_csv(path, header=None)\\n    if df.shape[1] >= 4:\\n        df = df.iloc[:, :4]\\n        df.columns = cols\\n    else:\\n        df.columns = cols[:df.shape[1]]\\n    if \'rating\' in df.columns:\\n        df = df[df[\'rating\'] > 3][[\'user\', \'item\']].copy()\\n    else:\\n        df = df[[\'user\', \'item\']].copy()\\n    return k_core_filter(df, min_k=MIN_CORE)\\n\\n\\ndef load_lastfm(path=\'UserTaggedArtists-timestamps.dat\'):\\n    df = pd.read_csv(path, sep=\'\\\\t\')\\n    cols = {c.lower(): c for c in df.columns}\\n    user_col = cols.get(\'userid\', df.columns[0])\\n    item_col = cols.get(\'artistid\', df.columns[1])\\n    df = df[[user_col, item_col]].rename(columns={user_col: \'user\', item_col: \'item\'})\\n    return k_core_filter(df, min_k=MIN_CORE)\\n\\n\\ndef user_holdout_split(df, seed=42, test_ratio=0.2, user_col=\'user\', item_col=\'item\'):\\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\\n    test_parts = []\\n    train_parts = []\\n    for u, udf in df.groupby(user_col, sort=False):\\n        n = len(udf)\\n        if n < 2:\\n            train_parts.append(udf)\\n            continue\\n        n_test = max(1, int(round(n * test_ratio)))\\n        n_test = min(n_test, n - 1)\\n        idx = np.arange(n)\\n        test_idx = rng.choice(idx, size=n_test, replace=False)\\n        mask = np.zeros(n, dtype=bool)\\n        mask[test_idx] = True\\n        test_parts.append(udf.iloc[mask])\\n        train_parts.append(udf.iloc[~mask])\\n    train = pd.concat(train_parts, ignore_index=True)\\n    test = pd.concat(test_parts, ignore_index=True)\\n    return train, test\\n\\n\\ndef get_algo(name):\\n    if name == \'ALS\':\\n        return ImplicitMF(features=50, iterations=10, weight=40, progress=False)\\n    if name == \'ItemKNN\':\\n        return ItemItem(nnbrs=20, min_nbrs=1, center=False)\\n    if name == \'Pop\':\\n        return Popular()\\n    raise ValueError(name)\\n\\n\\ndef precision_at_k(rec_items, rel_set, k):\\n    if k == 0:\\n        return np.nan\\n    hits = sum(1 for i in rec_items[:k] if i in rel_set)\\n    return hits / k\\n\\n\\ndef ndcg_at_k(rec_items, rel_set, k):\\n    dcg = 0.0\\n    for rank, item in enumerate(rec_items[:k], start=1):\\n        if item in rel_set:\\n            dcg += 1.0 / np.log2(rank + 1)\\n    ideal = sum(1.0 / np.log2(r + 1) for r in range(1, min(len(rel_set), k) + 1))\\n    return dcg / ideal if ideal > 0 else np.nan\\n\\n\\ndef evaluate_batch(recs, test_df, ks=KS):\\n    truth = test_df.groupby(\'user\')[\'item\'].apply(set)\\n    rec_map = recs.groupby(\'user\')[\'item\'].apply(list)\\n    users = sorted(set(truth.index).intersection(rec_map.index))\\n    rows = []\\n    for u in users:\\n        rel = truth[u]\\n        rlist = rec_map[u]\\n        row = {\'user\': u}\\n        for k in ks:\\n            row[f\'Precision@{k}\'] = precision_at_k(rlist, rel, k)\\n            row[f\'nDCG@{k}\'] = ndcg_at_k(rlist, rel, k)\\n        rows.append(row)\\n    udf = pd.DataFrame(rows)\\n    return udf, udf.drop(columns=[\'user\']).mean().to_dict()\\n\\n\\ndef plot_variability(results, dataset_name):\\n    metrics = [f\'nDCG@{k}\' for k in KS] + [f\'Precision@{k}\' for k in KS]\\n    fig, axes = plt.subplots(2, 3, figsize=(13, 7), constrained_layout=True)\\n    axes = axes.ravel()\\n    for ax, metric in zip(axes, metrics):\\n        pivot = results.pivot_table(index=\'seed\', columns=\'algorithm\', values=metric)\\n        for col in pivot.columns:\\n            ax.plot(pivot.index, pivot[col], marker=\'o\', label=col)\\n        ax.set_title(metric)\\n        ax.set_xlabel(\'seed\')\\n        ax.set_ylabel(metric)\\n    handles, labels = axes[0].get_legend_handles_labels()\\n    if handles:\\n        fig.legend(handles, labels, loc=\'upper center\', ncol=3)\\n    fig.suptitle(f\'Seed sensitivity: {dataset_name}\')\\n    fig.savefig(os.path.join(working_dir, f\'{dataset_name}_seed_variability.png\'), dpi=150)\\n    plt.close(fig)\\n\\n\\ndatasets = {\\n    \'ml100k\': load_ml100k(\'u.data\'),\\n    \'amazon_vg\': load_amazon(\'VideoGames.csv\'),\\n    \'lastfm\': load_lastfm(\'UserTaggedArtists-timestamps.dat\'),\\n}\\n\\nall_results = []\\n\\nfor dname, data in datasets.items():\\n    print(f\'Loaded {dname}: {len(data):,} interactions, {data.user.nunique():,} users, {data.item.nunique():,} items\')\\n    experiment_data[dname][\'ground_truth\'] = data[[\'user\', \'item\']].to_dict(\'records\')[:1000]\\n    for seed in SEEDS:\\n        train, test = user_holdout_split(data, seed=seed, test_ratio=0.2)\\n        users = test[\'user\'].drop_duplicates()\\n        for aname in [\'ALS\', \'ItemKNN\', \'Pop\']:\\n            algo = get_algo(aname)\\n            algo.fit(train)\\n            print(f\'Dataset={dname} Seed={seed} Algo={aname}: validation_loss = {float(\\"nan\\"):.4f}\')\\n            recs = recommend(algo, users, TOPN)\\n            recs = recs[[\'user\', \'item\', \'rank\']].copy()\\n            user_metrics, agg = evaluate_batch(recs, test, ks=KS)\\n            row = {\'dataset\': dname, \'seed\': seed, \'algorithm\': aname}\\n            row.update(agg)\\n            all_results.append(row)\\n            experiment_data[dname][\'metrics\'][\'val\'].append({\'seed\': seed, \'algorithm\': aname, **agg})\\n            experiment_data[dname][\'losses\'][\'val\'].append({\'seed\': seed, \'algorithm\': aname, \'validation_loss\': np.nan})\\n            experiment_data[dname][\'predictions\'].append({\'seed\': seed, \'algorithm\': aname, \'n_recs\': len(recs)})\\n            np.save(os.path.join(working_dir, f\'{dname}_{aname}_seed{seed}_user_metrics.npy\'), user_metrics.to_dict(\'records\'))\\n            print(pd.Series(row).to_string())\\n\\nresults = pd.DataFrame(all_results)\\nresults.to_csv(os.path.join(working_dir, \'seed_sensitivity_results.csv\'), index=False)\\nnp.save(os.path.join(working_dir, \'