[2026/07/16 10:42:24] [DEBUG] isgsa.llm: prompt content: {'Introduction': 'You are an experienced recommender systems researcher. Your previous code for research experiment had a bug, so based on the information below, you should revise it in order to fix this bug. Your response should be an implementation outline in natural language, followed by a single markdown code block which implements the bugfix/solution.', 'Research task': " You are an expert recommender systems research assistant who is looking to help the user with their requests.\nThe user has some idea and you want to conduct creative experiments to gain scientific insights.\nYour aim is to run experiments to gather sufficient results to report back to the user.\nThe idea is:\n\nI'd like to run an experiment to quantify how much data split random seeds affect recommender system accuracy. Please use LensKit 0.14.4 to test three algorithms: ALS, ItemKNN, and Pop. Run this on the following three datasets with implicit feedback: MovieLens100K, Amazon Video Games, Last.FM. The raw files are stored in your working directory with the filenames u.data, VideoGames.csv, UserTaggedArtists-timestamps.dat. First, preprocess all datasets with 5-core filtering. For the Amazon and MovieLens datasets, please also convert any ratings greater than 3 to implicit interactions. Here's the main experimental procedure: Generate 5 different random seeds for data splitting. For each algorithm, dataset, and seed, please do a user-based 80/20 holdout split. Train all models using standard hyperparameters. For the analysis, I need you to measure nDCG@k and Precision@k for k=1, 5, 10 and conduct a short statistical analysis. Please use batch recommendation for all users at once instead of per-user loops for efficiency.", 'Previous (buggy) implementation': "```python\nimport os\nworking_dir = os.path.join(os.getcwd(), 'working')\nos.makedirs(working_dir, exist_ok=True)\n\nimport warnings\nwarnings.filterwarnings('ignore')\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nfrom scipy import stats\n\nfrom lenskit.algorithms.basic import Popular\nfrom lenskit.algorithms.als import ImplicitMF\nfrom lenskit.algorithms.item_knn import ItemItem\nfrom lenskit.batch import recommend\n\nexperiment_data = {\n    'ml100k': {'metrics': {'train': [], 'val': []}, 'losses': {'train': [], 'val': []}, 'predictions': [], 'ground_truth': []},\n    'amazon_videogames': {'metrics': {'train': [], 'val': []}, 'losses': {'train': [], 'val': []}, 'predictions': [], 'ground_truth': []},\n    'lastfm': {'metrics': {'train': [], 'val': []}, 'losses': {'train': [], 'val': []}, 'predictions': [], 'ground_truth': []},\n}\n\nseeds = [1, 7, 21, 42, 84]\nks = [1, 5, 10]\n\n\ndef kcore_filter(df, user_col='user', item_col='item', min_uc=5, min_ic=5):\n    df = df[[user_col, item_col]].drop_duplicates().copy()\n    while True:\n        ucnt = df.groupby(user_col)[item_col].transform('size')\n        icnt = df.groupby(item_col)[user_col].transform('size')\n        ndf = df[(ucnt >= min_uc) & (icnt >= min_ic)].copy()\n        if len(ndf) == len(df):\n            break\n        df = ndf\n    return df.reset_index(drop=True)\n\n\ndef load_ml100k(path='u.data'):\n    df = pd.read_csv(path, sep='\\t', header=None, names=['user', 'item', 'rating', 'ts'])\n    df = df[df['rating'] > 3][['user', 'item']].copy()\n    return kcore_filter(df)\n\n\ndef load_amazon(path='VideoGames.csv'):\n    df = pd.read_csv(path, header=None)\n    if df.shape[1] >= 3:\n        df = df.iloc[:, :3].copy()\n        df.columns = ['user', 'item', 'rating']\n    else:\n        raise ValueError('VideoGames.csv must have at least 3 columns: user,item,rating')\n    df = df[df['rating'] > 3][['user', 'item']].copy()\n    return kcore_filter(df)\n\n\ndef load_lastfm(path='UserTaggedArtists-timestamps.dat'):\n    df = pd.read_csv(path, sep='\\t')\n    cols = {c.lower(): c for c in df.columns}\n    user_col = cols.get('userid', list(df.columns)[0])\n    item_col = cols.get('artistid', list(df.columns)[1])\n    df = df[[user_col, item_col]].copy()\n    df.columns = ['user', 'item']\n    return kcore_filter(df)\n\n\ndef user_holdout(df, seed, test_ratio=0.2):\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n    train_parts, test_parts = [], []\n    for u, udf in df.groupby('user', sort=False):\n        n = len(udf)\n        if n < 2:\n            train_parts.append(udf)\n            continue\n        n_test = max(1, int(round(n * test_ratio)))\n        idx = np.arange(n)\n        test_idx = rng.choice(idx, size=min(n_test, n - 1), replace=False)\n        mask = np.zeros(n, dtype=bool)\n        mask[test_idx] = True\n        test_parts.append(udf.iloc[mask])\n        train_parts.append(udf.iloc[~mask])\n    train = pd.concat(train_parts, ignore_index=True)\n    test = pd.concat(test_parts, ignore_index=True)\n    return train, test\n\n\ndef precision_at_k(rec_items, truth, k):\n    if len(rec_items) == 0:\n        return 0.0\n    topk = rec_items[:k]\n    return len(set(topk) & truth) / float(k)\n\n\ndef ndcg_at_k(rec_items, truth, k):\n    topk = rec_items[:k]\n    if not truth:\n        return 0.0\n    gains = np.array([1.0 if i in truth else 0.0 for i in topk], dtype=float)\n    if gains.size == 0:\n        return 0.0\n    discounts = 1.0 / np.log2(np.arange(2, gains.size + 2))\n    dcg = np.sum(gains * discounts)\n    ideal_len = min(k, len(truth))\n    idcg = np.sum(1.0 / np.log2(np.arange(2, ideal_len + 2)))\n    return float(dcg / idcg) if idcg > 0 else 0.0\n\n\ndef evaluate_batch(algo, train, test, name, dname, seed):\n    algo.fit(train)\n    users = test['user'].drop_duplicates().tolist()\n    recs = recommend(algo, users, 10)\n    truth = test.groupby('user')['item'].apply(set).to_dict()\n    rows = []\n    pred_pack = {}\n    for u, udf in recs.groupby('user', sort=False):\n        items = udf.sort_values('rank')['item'].tolist()\n        pred_pack[u] = items\n        gt = truth.get(u, set())\n        row = {'user': u}\n        for k in ks:\n            row[f'precision@{k}'] = precision_at_k(items, gt, k)\n            row[f'ndcg@{k}'] = ndcg_at_k(items, gt, k)\n        rows.append(row)\n    mdf = pd.DataFrame(rows)\n    agg = mdf.drop(columns=['user']).mean().to_dict() if len(mdf) else {f'{m}@{k}': 0.0 for m in ['precision', 'ndcg'] for k in ks}\n    print(f'[{dname}][{name}][seed={seed}] validation_loss = nan')\n    print(f'[{dname}][{name}][seed={seed}] ' + ', '.join([f'{k}={v:.4f}' for k, v in agg.items()]))\n    return agg, recs, truth, mdf\n\n\ndef make_algorithms():\n    return {\n        'ALS': ImplicitMF(features=32, iterations=10, reg=0.1, weight=40),\n        'ItemKNN': ItemItem(20, center=False),\n        'Pop': Popular(),\n    }\n\n\ndatasets = {\n    'ml100k': load_ml100k('u.data'),\n    'amazon_videogames': load_amazon('VideoGames.csv'),\n    'lastfm': load_lastfm('UserTaggedArtists-timestamps.dat'),\n}\n\nall_results = []\nseed_summaries = []\nfor dname, df in datasets.items():\n    for seed in seeds:\n        train, test = user_holdout(df, seed, 0.2)\n        algos = make_algorithms()\n        for aname, algo in algos.items():\n            metrics, recs, truth, user_metrics = evaluate_batch(algo, train, test, aname, dname, seed)\n            row = {'dataset': dname, 'algorithm': aname, 'seed': seed, 'n_train': len(train), 'n_test': len(test)}\n            row.update(metrics)\n            all_results.append(row)\n            experiment_data[dname]['metrics']['val'].append({'seed': seed, 'algorithm': aname, **metrics})\n            experiment_data[dname]['losses']['val'].append({'seed': seed, 'algorithm': aname, 'validation_loss': np.nan})\n            experiment_data[dname]['predictions'].append({'seed': seed, 'algorithm': aname, 'recs': recs.to_dict('list')})\n            experiment_data[dname]['ground_truth'].append({'seed': seed, 'algorithm': aname, 'truth': {str(k): list(v) for k, v in truth.items()}})\n            np.save(os.path.join(working_dir, f'{dname}_{aname}_seed{seed}_user_metrics.npy'), user_metrics.to_dict('records'))\n\nresults_df = pd.DataFrame(all_results)\nresults_df.to_csv(os.path.join(working_dir, 'seed_sensitivity_results.csv'), index=False)\nnp.save(os.path.join(working_dir, 'seed_sensitivity_results.npy'), results_df.to_dict('records'))\n\nfor (dname, aname), g in results_df.groupby(['dataset', 'algorithm']):\n    summary = {'dataset': dname, 'algorithm': aname}\n    for metric in [f'precision@{k}' for k in ks] + [f'ndcg@{k}' for k in ks]:\n        vals = g[metric].values.astype(float)\n        summary[f'{metric}_mean'] = vals.mean()\n        summary[f'{metric}_std'] = vals.std(ddof=1) if len(vals) > 1 else 0.0\n        summary[f'{metric}_cv'] = (summary[f'{metric}_std'] / summary[f'{metric}_mean']) if summary[f'{metric}_mean'] != 0 else np.nan\n    seed_summaries.append(summary)\n\nsummary_df = pd.DataFrame(seed_summaries)\nsummary_df.to_csv(os.path.join(working_dir, 'seed_sensitivity_summary.csv'), index=False)\nnp.save(os.path.join(working_dir, 'seed_sensitivity_summary.npy'), summary_df.to_dict('records'))\n\nanova_rows = []\nfor dname in results_df['dataset'].unique():\n    for metric in [f'precision@{k}' for k in ks] + [f'ndcg@{k}' for k in ks]:\n        groups = [g[metric].values for _, g in results_df[results_df['dataset'] == dname].groupby('algorithm')]\n        if len(groups) >= 2 and all(len(x) > 1 for x in groups):\n            fstat, pval = stats.f_oneway(*groups)\n        else:\n            fstat, pval = np.nan, np.nan\n        anova_rows.append({'dataset': dname, 'metric': metric, 'F_algorithms': fstat, 'p_value': pval})\n\nanova_df = pd.DataFrame(anova_rows)\nanova_df.to_csv(os.path.join(working_dir, 'algorithm_anova_by_dataset.csv'), index=False)\nnp.save(os.path.join(working_dir, 'algorithm_anova_by_dataset.npy'), anova_df.to_dict('records'))\n\nfor dname in results_df['dataset'].unique():\n    fig, axes = plt.subplots(2, 3, figsize=(12, 6), sharex=True)\n    metrics_order =