[2026/07/16 11:11:23] [DEBUG] isgsa.llm: prompt content: {'Introduction': 'You are an expert recommender systems researcher conducting a code review. Your task is to evaluate whether the code execution was successful or contains bugs. Focus on identifying execution failures, errors, or other issues that would prevent the code from working properly.', 'Research Task': " You are an expert recommender systems research assistant who is looking to help the user with their requests.\nThe user has some idea and you want to conduct creative experiments to gain scientific insights.\nYour aim is to run experiments to gather sufficient results to report back to the user.\nThe idea is:\n\nI'd like to run an experiment to quantify how much data split random seeds affect recommender system accuracy. Please use LensKit 0.14.4 to test three algorithms: ALS, ItemKNN, and Pop. Run this on the following three datasets with implicit feedback: MovieLens100K, Amazon Video Games, Last.FM. The raw files are stored in your working directory with the filenames u.data, VideoGames.csv, UserTaggedArtists-timestamps.dat. First, preprocess all datasets with 5-core filtering. For the Amazon and MovieLens datasets, please also convert any ratings greater than 3 to implicit interactions. Here's the main experimental procedure: Generate 5 different random seeds for data splitting. For each algorithm, dataset, and seed, please do a user-based 80/20 holdout split. Train all models using standard hyperparameters. For the analysis, I need you to measure nDCG@k and Precision@k for k=1, 5, 10 and conduct a short statistical analysis. Please use batch recommendation for all users at once instead of per-user loops for efficiency.", 'Implementation': '```python\nimport os\nworking_dir = os.path.join(os.getcwd(), \'working\')\nos.makedirs(working_dir, exist_ok=True)\n\nimport warnings\nwarnings.filterwarnings(\'ignore\')\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\nfrom lenskit import batch\nfrom lenskit.algorithms import Recommender\nfrom lenskit.algorithms.basic import Popular\nfrom lenskit.algorithms.als import ImplicitMF\nfrom lenskit.algorithms.item_knn import ItemItem\n\nexperiment_data = {\n    \'ml100k\': {\'metrics\': {\'train\': [], \'val\': []}, \'losses\': {\'train\': [], \'val\': []}, \'predictions\': [], \'ground_truth\': []},\n    \'amazon_videogames\': {\'metrics\': {\'train\': [], \'val\': []}, \'losses\': {\'train\': [], \'val\': []}, \'predictions\': [], \'ground_truth\': []},\n    \'lastfm\': {\'metrics\': {\'train\': [], \'val\': []}, \'losses\': {\'train\': [], \'val\': []}, \'predictions\': [], \'ground_truth\': []},\n}\n\nSEEDS = [1, 7, 21, 42, 84]\nKS = [1, 5, 10]\nMAX_K = max(KS)\nFILES = {\n    \'ml100k\': \'u.data\',\n    \'amazon_videogames\': \'VideoGames.csv\',\n    \'lastfm\': \'UserTaggedArtists-timestamps.dat\'\n}\n\n\ndef check_file(path):\n    if not os.path.exists(path):\n        raise FileNotFoundError(f\'Missing required file: {path}\')\n\n\ndef validate_nonempty(df, name):\n    if df is None or len(df) == 0:\n        raise ValueError(f\'{name} is empty after preprocessing\')\n    need = {\'user\', \'item\'}\n    miss = need - set(df.columns)\n    if miss:\n        raise ValueError(f\'{name} missing columns: {miss}\')\n\n\ndef k_core_filter(df, user_col=\'user\', item_col=\'item\', min_k=5):\n    df = df[[user_col, item_col]].dropna().drop_duplicates().copy()\n    if df.empty:\n        return df.rename(columns={user_col: \'user\', item_col: \'item\'})\n    df = df.rename(columns={user_col: \'user\', item_col: \'item\'})\n    while True:\n        uc = df[\'user\'].value_counts()\n        ic = df[\'item\'].value_counts()\n        keep_u = uc[uc >= min_k].index\n        keep_i = ic[ic >= min_k].index\n        new_df = df[df[\'user\'].isin(keep_u) & df[\'item\'].isin(keep_i)]\n        if len(new_df) == len(df):\n            break\n        df = new_df\n        if df.empty:\n            break\n    return df.reset_index(drop=True)\n\n\ndef load_ml100k(path):\n    check_file(path)\n    df = pd.read_csv(path, sep=\'\\t\', header=None, names=[\'user\', \'item\', \'rating\', \'timestamp\'])\n    df = df[df[\'rating\'] > 3][[\'user\', \'item\']]\n    df = k_core_filter(df)\n    validate_nonempty(df, \'ml100k\')\n    return df\n\n\ndef load_amazon(path):\n    check_file(path)\n    raw = pd.read_csv(path)\n    cols = {c.lower(): c for c in raw.columns}\n    ucol = cols.get(\'user_id\') or cols.get(\'userid\') or cols.get(\'reviewerid\')\n    icol = cols.get(\'item_id\') or cols.get(\'asin\')\n    rcol = cols.get(\'rating\') or cols.get(\'overall\')\n    if not (ucol and icol and rcol):\n        raise ValueError(f\'Amazon schema not recognized: {list(raw.columns)}\')\n    df = raw[[ucol, icol, rcol]].rename(columns={ucol: \'user\', icol: \'item\', rcol: \'rating\'})\n    df = df[df[\'rating\'] > 3][[\'user\', \'item\']]\n    df = k_core_filter(df)\n    validate_nonempty(df, \'amazon_videogames\')\n    return df\n\n\ndef load_lastfm(path):\n    check_file(path)\n    df = pd.read_csv(path, sep=\'\\t\')\n    cols = {c.lower(): c for c in df.columns}\n    ucol = cols.get(\'userid\')\n    icol = cols.get(\'artistid\')\n    if not (ucol and icol):\n        raise ValueError(f\'LastFM schema not recognized: {list(df.columns)}\')\n    df = df[[ucol, icol]].rename(columns={ucol: \'user\', icol: \'item\'})\n    df = k_core_filter(df)\n    validate_nonempty(df, \'lastfm\')\n    return df\n\n\ndef user_holdout_split(df, seed=42, test_frac=0.2):\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n    train_parts, test_parts = [], []\n    eval_users = 0\n    for _, udf in df.groupby(\'user\', sort=False):\n        n = len(udf)\n        if n < 2:\n            continue\n        n_test = max(1, int(np.floor(n * test_frac)))\n        n_test = min(n_test, n - 1)\n        idx = np.arange(n)\n        test_idx = rng.choice(idx, size=n_test, replace=False)\n        mask = np.zeros(n, dtype=bool)\n        mask[test_idx] = True\n        tr = udf.iloc[~mask]\n        te = udf.iloc[mask]\n        if len(tr) > 0 and len(te) > 0:\n            train_parts.append(tr)\n            test_parts.append(te)\n            eval_users += 1\n    if eval_users == 0:\n        raise ValueError(\'No users support the holdout protocol\')\n    train = pd.concat(train_parts, ignore_index=True)\n    test = pd.concat(test_parts, ignore_index=True)\n    return train, test, eval_users\n\n\ndef build_algorithms():\n    return {\n        \'ALS\': Recommender.adapt(ImplicitMF()),\n        \'ItemKNN\': Recommender.adapt(ItemItem()),\n        \'Pop\': Recommender.adapt(Popular())\n    }\n\n\ndef metric_from_recs(recs_df, truth_map, k):\n    rec_k = recs_df[recs_df[\'rank\'] <= k]\n    rec_map = rec_k.groupby(\'user\')[\'item\'].apply(list).to_dict()\n    pvals, ndcgvals = [], []\n    for u, truth in truth_map.items():\n        ranked = rec_map.get(u, [])\n        hits = sum(1 for it in ranked if it in truth)\n        pvals.append(hits / k)\n        dcg = sum((1.0 / np.log2(i + 2)) for i, it in enumerate(ranked) if it in truth)\n        ideal = min(len(truth), k)\n        idcg = sum(1.0 / np.log2(i + 2) for i in range(ideal))\n        ndcgvals.append(dcg / idcg if idcg > 0 else 0.0)\n    return float(np.mean(pvals)), float(np.mean(ndcgvals))\n\n\ndef evaluate_algo(algo, train, test, ks):\n    truth = test.groupby(\'user\')[\'item\'].apply(set).to_dict()\n    users = list(truth.keys())\n    seen = train.groupby(\'user\')[\'item\'].apply(set).to_dict()\n    algo.fit(train)\n    try:\n        recs = batch.recommend(algo, users, n=MAX_K + 100, candidates=None)\n    except TypeError:\n        recs = batch.recommend(algo, users, n=MAX_K + 100)\n    if recs is None or len(recs) == 0:\n        raise ValueError(\'No recommendations returned\')\n    recs = recs.sort_values([\'user\', \'rank\']).copy()\n    recs = recs[~recs.apply(lambda r: r[\'item\'] in seen.get(r[\'user\'], set()), axis=1)]\n    recs[\'rank2\'] = recs.groupby(\'user\').cumcount() + 1\n    recs = recs[recs[\'rank2\'] <= MAX_K][[\'user\', \'item\', \'rank2\']].rename(columns={\'rank2\': \'rank\'})\n    out = []\n    for k in ks:\n        p, n = metric_from_recs(recs, truth, k)\n        out += [\n            {\'metric_name\': \'Precision\', \'k\': k, \'score\': p},\n            {\'metric_name\': \'nDCG\', \'k\': k, \'score\': n}\n        ]\n    return pd.DataFrame(out), recs, truth\n\n\ndatasets = {}\nfor name, path in FILES.items():\n    try:\n        datasets[name] = {\'ml100k\': load_ml100k, \'amazon_videogames\': load_amazon, \'lastfm\': load_lastfm}[name](path)\n        df = datasets[name]\n        print(f\'Loaded {name}: {len(df)} interactions, {df.user.nunique()} users, {df.item.nunique()} items\')\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\'Failed loading {name}: {e}\')\n\nall_results = []\nfailed_runs = []\nfor dname, df in datasets.items():\n    for seed in SEEDS:\n        try:\n            train, test, eval_users = user_holdout_split(df, seed=seed, test_frac=0.2)\n        except Exception as e:\n            failed_runs.append({\'dataset\': dname, \'seed\': seed, \'algorithm\': None, \'error\': str(e)})\n            continue\n        for aname, algo in build_algorithms().items():\n            print(f\'Epoch {seed}: validation_loss = {float("nan"):.4f}\')\n            try:\n                met_df, recs, truth = evaluate_algo(algo, train, test, KS)\n                ts = pd.Timestamp.now().isoformat()\n                met_df[\'dataset\'] = dname\n                met_df[\'algorithm\'] = aname\n                met_df[\'seed\'] = seed\n                met_df[\'evaluation_user_count\'] = eval_users\n                met_df[\'timestamp\'] = ts\n                all_results.append(met_df)\n                experiment_data[dname][\'metrics\'][\'train\'].append({\'seed\': seed, \'algorithm\': aname, \'n_train\': len(train), \'timestamp\': ts})\n                experiment_data[dname][\'metrics\'][\'val\'].append(met_df.to_dict(\'records\'))\n                experiment_data[dname][\'losses\'][\'train\'].append({\'seed\': seed, \'algorithm\': aname, \'loss\': np.nan, \'timestamp\': ts})\n                experiment_data[dname][\'losses\'][\'val\'].append({\'seed\': seed, \'algorithm\': aname, \'loss\': np.nan, \'timestamp\': ts})\n                experiment_data[dname][\'predictions\'].append({\'seed\': seed, \'algorithm\': aname, \'rows\': recs.to_dict(\'records\')})\n                experiment_data[dname][\'ground_truth\'].append({\'seed\': seed, \'algorithm\': aname, \'truth\': {str(k): list(v) for k, v in truth.items()}})\n                pretty = met_df[[\'metric_name\', \'k\', \'score\']].copy()\n                pretty[\'mk\'] = pretty[\'metric_name\'] + \'@\' + pretty[\'k\'].astype(str)\n                print(dname, aname, seed, dict(zip(pretty[\'mk\'], pretty[\'score\'].round(4))))\n            except Exception as e:\n                failed_runs.append({\'dataset\': dname, \'seed\': seed, \'algorithm\': aname, \'error\': str(e)})\n                print(f\'Run failed: {dname} {aname} seed={seed}: {e}\')\n\nresults = pd.concat(all_results, ignore_index=True) if all_results else pd.DataFrame(columns=[\'dataset\',\'algorithm\',\'seed\',\'metric_name\',\'k\',\'score\',\'evaluation_user_count\',\'timestamp\'])\nresults = results[[\'dataset\',\'algorithm\',\'seed\',\'metric_name\',\'k\',\'score\',\'evaluation_user_count\',\'timestamp\']]\nresults.to_csv(os.path.join(working_dir, \'seed_sensitivity_results_tidy.csv\'), index=False)\nnp.save(os.path.join(working_dir, \'experiment_data.npy\'), experiment_data, allow_pickle=True)\nnp.save(os.path.join(working_dir, \'results_array.npy\'), results.to_records(index=False), allow_pickle=True)\n\nif len(results):\n    summary = results.groupby([\'dataset\',\'algorithm\',\'metric_name\',\'k\']).agg(\n        mean_score=(\'score\',\'mean\'),\n        std_score=(\'score\',\'std\'),\n        min_score=(\'score\',\'min\'),\n        max_score=(\'score\',\'max\'),\n        evaluation_user_count=(\'evaluation_user_count\',\'max\'),\n        n_seeds=(\'seed\',\'nunique\')\n    ).reset_index()\n    summary[\'cv\'] = summary[\'std_score\'] / summary[\'mean_score\'].replace(0, np.nan)\n    summary.to_csv(os.path.join(working_dir, \'metric_summary_seed_sensitivity.csv\'), index=False)\n    np.save(os.path.join(working_dir, \'summary_records.npy\'), summary.to_records(index=False), allow_pickle=True)\n\n    wide = results.assign(metric=lambda x: x[\'metric_name\'] + \'@\' + x[\'k\'].astype(str)).pivot_table(\n        index=[\'dataset\',\'algorithm\',\'seed\',\'evaluation_user_count\'], columns=\'metric\', values=\'score\'\n    ).reset_index()\n    wide.to_csv(os.path.join(working_dir, \'seed_sensitivity_results_wide.csv\'), index=False)\n\n    most_sensitive = summary.sort_values([\'cv\',\'std_score\'], ascending=False).head(10)\n    print(\'\\nSeed sensitivity summary (top 10 by CV):\')\n    print(most_sensitive[[\'dataset\',\'algorithm\',\'metric_name\',\'k\',\'mean_score\',\'std_score\',\'cv\',\'min_score\',\'max_score\',\'n_seeds\']].to_string(index=False))\n\n    print(\'\\nPer-run tidy results:\')\n    print(results[[\'dataset\',\'algorithm\',\'seed\',\'metric_name\',\'k\',\'score\',\'evaluation_user_count\']].to_string(index=False))\nelse:\n    summary = pd.DataFrame()\n    print(\'No successful runs.\')\n\nfail_df = pd.DataFrame(failed_runs)\nfail_df.to_csv(os.path.join(working_dir, \'failed_runs.csv\'), index=False)\nnp.save(os.path.join(working_dir, \'failed_runs.npy\'), fail_df.to_records(index=False) if len(fail_df) else np.array([]), allow_pickle=True)\nprint(\'\\nFailed runs:\', 0 if fail_df is None else len(fail_df))\nprint(\'Done. Files saved to:\', working_dir)\n```', 'Execution Output': '```\nLoaded ml100k: 54413 interactions, 938 users, 1008 items\nFailed loading amazon_videogames: Amazon schema not recognized: [\'user_id\', \'parent_asin\', \'rating\', \'timestamp\']\nLoaded lastfm: 52551 interactions, 1090 users, 3646 items